      players: 'One player. Pas Seul is a single-player patience (solitaire) game.',
      deck: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck. One deck. No jokers.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck and table space for stock, waste, six tableau piles, and four foundations.',
      dealing: 'Layout: Place four foundation spaces (upper right). Six tableau piles (main stacks) below. Stock (closed deck) upper left; waste pile next to it. Deal one card face-up to each of the six tableau piles to start (or per variant). Remaining cards form the stock. Only one pass through the stock is allowed.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Turn a card from the stock onto the waste; only the topmost card of the waste may be played. 2. The top waste card may be moved to a foundation (build up in suit from Ace to King) or to a tableau pile. 3. On the tableau, build down in alternating colors; any card may be placed on an empty tableau pile. 4. You may move one or more cards from one tableau pile to another when the build rule holds. 5. Only one pass through the stock is allowed; there is no redeal.',
